      "description": "Watch Cardiff City vs Wroxham highlights and goals from Championship on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on August 17, 2026. The Championship clash between Cardiff City and Wrexham delivered a masterclass in tension, with both sides searching for a decisive edge under the floodlights. Fans were treated to a display of grit and tactical discipline that kept the result in doubt until the referee's final whistle. Early Breakthrough for the Visitors On August 17, 2026 , the atmosphere was electric as the match got underway, but the home crowd was stunned just minutes into the contest. In the 3rd minute, Wrexham took full advantage of an early opening to seize the lead. Daniel Imray provided a clinical assist for Kieffer Moore , who made no mistake in finding the back of the net. This early goal forced Cardiff City to rethink their strategy immediately, as they spent much of the first half struggling to break down a well-organized visiting defense. Midfield Attrition and Tactical Shifts The game grew increasingly physical as the minutes ticked by, with the referee busy managing several heated exchanges. Kieffer Moore picked up a yellow card in the 33rd minute, and the intensity didn't drop after the break, as Dominic Hyam also went into the book in the 54th minute. In a bid to change the momentum, Cardiff City introduced Rubin Colwill for Ollie Tanner just past the hour mark. Both managers utilized their benches heavily in the final twenty minutes, leading to a fragmented but high-stakes conclusion to the match. Stoppage Time Drama As the game entered the dying moments, it appeared Wrexham would hold on for a narrow victory. However, the narrative shifted dramatically in the 8th minute of stoppage time. Rubin Colwill , who had been lively since coming on, struck a sensational late goal to level the score at 1-1. The euphoria of the goal led to a yellow card for Colwill just moments later for his celebration, but the damage to the visitors was done. The final whistle blew shortly after, concluding a pulsating encounter where persistence finally paid off for the home side."
